WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.000
OK, breaking news, right?

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.430
It sounds like our activism worked.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:12.360
Donald Trump's postmaster general, Lewis Dejoy,
will be suspending reforms and initiatives

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.270
for the post office until after the November
election.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:22.560
According to a draft statement that Reuters
is reporting on, great news, right, Dejoy

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.070
says, I'm suspending these initiatives until
after the election.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:32.029
This is being done to avoid even the appearance
of impacting election related mail.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:33.960
We won, right, guys?

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.079
Except not so fast.

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:36.079
Not so fast at all.

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:37.220
This is not what it seems.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:43.059
This announcement is the post office will
not be changing retail hours.

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:47.289
Existing mail collection boxes will remain
where they are.

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:51.050
No more mail processing facilities will be
closed.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.870
But notice that absent is the answer to the
question.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.359
What happens to what you've already done?

00:00:56.359 --> 00:00:59.319
So there's a couple of different things here
that we have to talk about.

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:02.519
First of all, at some surface level, I mean,
okay, good.

00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:03.519
Right?

00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:04.519
I don't want it.

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:05.519
I don't want to dismiss this as nothing.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:10.880
The activism, the sounding, the alarm, the
pulling, the joy in to answer questions before

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.630
lawmakers, it led to an announcement that
more isn't going to be done.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.630
That's good, I guess.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:18.500
And and we should recognize that.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.170
But the reality is that the damage may have
already been done.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:26.759
The changes that they've made already have
been done in disproportionately blue areas

00:01:26.759 --> 00:01:29.920
to restrict delivery of mail, to create pileups.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.250
And his statement says nothing about.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.719
We're also going to undo all of the things
we've done in the last three weeks.

00:01:35.719 --> 00:01:40.140
It says they will be suspending future changes
until after the election.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:45.329
So I don't know about you, but I'm not particularly
reassured by this.

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:49.649
He may have already done what needed to be
done in the blue voting areas.

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:54.530
And this could be an announcement, in fact,
to give a false sense of security.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.100
So just remember, these people are not our
friends.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.590
We have no reason to trust them.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.569
He has done a huge amount of damage.

00:02:02.569 --> 00:02:05.130
Some sorting machines have been dismantled.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.490
Some collection boxes have been closed.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:13.150
So the idea that this is a victory of accountability
where we now don't have to worry about this,

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.150
we fixed it.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:15.150
We won, guys.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.240
Now everything's fine with the mail for the
purposes of the upcoming election.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.620
It ignores reality.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:26.080
And I don't think I'm being too cynical by
saying this, although if you think I am.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.220
Let me know.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:32.690
The other part of this that really needs to
be restated is that this announcement is not

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:39.150
a license to say I now don't need to worry
and I'll just send my absentee ballot the

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.970
day before the election and be confident that
it's going to be counted again.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:48.471
They are not undoing the damage that they
have already done, as far as we can tell and

00:02:48.471 --> 00:02:50.640
as far as has been stated so far.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:56.160
So if it were me and I am in this position
in the sense that I'm voting absentee and

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.530
I will have to make a decision about how and
when I send in my ballot, I would return the

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.600
ballot as soon as possible.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.980
If you're mailing it, if you have the ability
to drive it to a ballot box, I would do that

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:09.980
as well.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.380
And that's actually my plan here in Massachusetts.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:17.550
I will be bringing my ballot to city hall
if I ever get it.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:22.150
I told the story yesterday of how I actually
still have not received my ballot for the

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.060
primary, which is September one.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.600
I requested it at this point.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.640
Something like 13, 14 days ago.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.760
And I would encourage other people to just
make sure you have a plan that makes sense

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.200
based on what's happening in your state, based
on where you can drop off ballots in your

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.200
state.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.010
And don't make your plan on the basis of a
false sense of security from this announcement.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.570
That's the most important message.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:50.160
I think they have done a bunch of stuff and
now they're trying to get everybody to forget

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.870
about this by saying, hey, you know what?

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:58.210
To avoid the appearance of of maybe affecting
election mail, we're not going to be making

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.980
any more changes.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.210
Well, they've already done a bunch of stuff.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.840
We just don't know the full extent of it.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:08.350
We don't know the full extent of what's been
taken off line.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.120
So we we just can't chance it is the point.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:16.560
And at the end of the show today, during the
voice mail segment, I am going to be talking

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.560
a little.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:23.040
More about the ballot off situation and how
it really varies from state to state, and

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.620
of course, that also makes this complicated,
where a country of 50 states plus D.C. plus

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.730
some territories.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:38.240
And we have 50 different election systems,
essentially with dramatically different rules

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:43.510
in each state in terms of how primaries and
elections are done, where ballots can be dropped

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.510
off.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.510
And so much more.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:48.009
So I'm going to address that a little bit
more later in the program.

